From e8cf1a1a25e3091baf88cbe28104c307424b7134 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 16:01:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0258 -- #38: fix GUS SFX-init quit-to-DOS (missing
 'skipped' summary arg)

The initGusSfx() completion summary LOG_INFO has 5 {} placeholders but passed
only 4 args (uploaded, NUM_SOUNDS, failed, used_kb) -- the 'skipped' count was
omitted (args jump from 'failed' straight to 'used_kb'). The DJGPP logger routes
the format string through fmt::format_to as a RUNTIME format (not FMT_STRING),
so it is NOT a compile error; at runtime fmt throws format_error("argument not
found"), uncaught on DJGPP -> std::terminate -> quit-to-DOS.

Why DOS needs this: on DJGPP a fmt runtime-format arg-count mismatch is a hard
terminate (uncaught exception), not a silent truncation. It fires the instant
the SFX upload loop finishes -- deterministic, RENDERSAFE-independent -- which
IS the #38 crash, and why SFX_OFF=1 (initGusSfx skipped) always dodged it. g2k
wave-gussfx2 logs (GSF2A/GSF2B) show the loop completing to the last slot fx75
then dying before this summary ever prints. Fix: pass 'skipped' as the 4th arg.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/Pixtone.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp b/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp
index f7427a15..e8829930 100644
--- a/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/Pixtone.cpp
@@ -849,7 +849,7 @@ bool Pixtone::initGusSfx()
            "Persistent SFX bank = {} KB DRAM (the MidiBackendGus per-song .pat "
            "residency preserves it via its auto-snapshotted keep-mark at first "
            "song start; the reserve above it always fits a song's instruments).",
-           uploaded, (int)NUM_SOUNDS, failed, used_kb);
+           uploaded, (int)NUM_SOUNDS, failed, skipped, used_kb);
   return uploaded > 0;
 }
 
